# Tests for subset.sem: every invariant of `checkSubset` and `diagnose` is
# verified below, on the squares sample (samples/squares/squares.sem) and on
# copies of it changed to step outside the subset in one place each.

collectTest is test
collectTest purpose "The squares sample is accepted, and its values, calls, labels, and steps are collected"
collectTest verifies checkSubset collectsProgram
collectTest typeParameter none
collectTest input none
collectTest output none
collectTest outputOwnedBy none
collectTest raises none
collectTest effect none
collectTest uses none
collectTest memoryHeap true
collectTest async false
collectTest maxRecursion none
collectTest label begin loopKind none
collectTest label begin within none
collectTest label lexed loopKind none
collectTest label lexed within none
collectTest label grouped loopKind none
collectTest label grouped within none
collectTest label modelled loopKind none
collectTest label modelled within none
collectTest label counts loopKind none
collectTest label counts within none
collectTest label limitFound loopKind none
collectTest label limitFound within none
collectTest label loopFound loopKind none
collectTest label loopFound within none
collectTest label printFound loopKind none
collectTest label printFound within none
collectTest label squareFound loopKind none
collectTest label squareFound within none
collectTest label refused loopKind none
collectTest label refused within none
collectTest let source String "# A stage0 sample: an arithmetic loop. It prints the squares of 1 to `limit`\n# (1, 4, 9, 16, 25), one per line, from a `while` loop bounded by the module\n# constant `limit`, and exits with code 0.\n\nsquares is module\nsquares purpose \"Print the squares of the whole numbers from 1 to a limit\"\nsquares path squares\nsquares imports standard.console\nsquares imports standard.math\nsquares imports standard.compare\nsquares exports main\n\nstdoutWriter is capability\nstdoutWriter purpose \"Authority to write lines to standard output\"\nstdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none\n\nlimit is constant\nlimit purpose \"The last number whose square is printed\"\nlimit type Int64\nlimit value 5\n\nmain is operation\nmain purpose \"Print the square of each whole number from 1 to the limit\"\nmain invariant none\nmain typeParameter none\nmain input none\nmain output ExitCode\nmain outputOwnedBy none\nmain raises none\nmain effect write console.stdout\nmain uses stdoutWriter\nmain memoryHeap false\nmain async false\nmain maxRecursion none\nmain label begin loopKind none\nmain label begin within none\nmain label nextSquare note \"Each pass prints one square; the loop returns to its header once per number\"\nmain label nextSquare loopKind while\nmain label nextSquare within none\nmain label nextSquare maxIterations limit\nmain label printSquare loopKind none\nmain label printSquare within nextSquare\nmain label advance loopKind none\nmain label advance within nextSquare\nmain label finished loopKind none\nmain label finished within none\nmain label failed loopKind none\nmain label failed within none\nmain let number Int64 1 mutable\nmain let one Int64 1 immutable\nmain let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable\nmain let failCode ExitCode 1 immutable\nmain at begin goto nextSquare\nmain at nextSquare do pastLimitCheck\nmain at nextSquare branch if pastLimit goto finished else goto printSquare\nmain at printSquare do square\nmain at printSquare do printIt\nmain at printSquare branch ifError printIt goto failed else goto advance\nmain at advance do addOne\nmain at advance set number nextNumber\nmain at advance goto nextSquare\nmain at finished return ok okCode\nmain at failed return ok failCode\n\npastLimitCheck is call\npastLimitCheck in main\npastLimitCheck invokes compare.greaterThanInt64\npastLimitCheck argument left Int64 number copy\npastLimitCheck argument right Int64 limit copy\npastLimitCheck result pastLimit Bool\npastLimitCheck ownedBy none\npastLimitCheck cleanedBy none\npastLimitCheck borrows none\npastLimitCheck catch none\npastLimitCheck suppresses none\n\nsquare is call\nsquare in main\nsquare invokes math.multiplyInt64\nsquare argument left Int64 number copy\nsquare argument right Int64 number copy\nsquare result squared Int64\nsquare ownedBy none\nsquare cleanedBy none\nsquare borrows none\nsquare catch none\nsquare suppresses none\n\nprintIt is call\nprintIt in main\nprintIt invokes console.writeIntegerLine\nprintIt argument value Int64 squared copy\nprintIt result none\nprintIt ownedBy none\nprintIt cleanedBy none\nprintIt borrows none\nprintIt catch printError console.WriteError\nprintIt suppresses none\n\naddOne is call\naddOne in main\naddOne invokes math.addInt64\naddOne argument left Int64 number copy\naddOne argument right Int64 one copy\naddOne result nextNumber Int64\naddOne ownedBy none\naddOne cleanedBy none\naddOne borrows none\naddOne catch none\naddOne suppresses none\n" immutable
collectTest let valueCount Int64 8 immutable
collectTest let callCount Int64 4 immutable
collectTest let labelCount Int64 6 immutable
collectTest let stepCount Int64 11 immutable
collectTest let constantOrigin Int64 1 immutable
collectTest let int64Type Int64 2 immutable
collectTest let two Int64 2 immutable
collectTest let limitName String "limit" immutable
collectTest let nextSquareName String "nextSquare" immutable
collectTest let printItName String "printIt" immutable
collectTest let squareName String "square" immutable
collectTest let refusedText String "the front end refused the source or a step failed" immutable
collectTest at begin do lex
collectTest at begin branch ifError lex goto refused else goto lexed
collectTest at lexed do newWords
collectTest at lexed do newRows
collectTest at lexed do group
collectTest at lexed branch ifError group goto refused else goto grouped
collectTest at grouped do newEntities
collectTest at grouped do newNames
collectTest at grouped do model
collectTest at grouped branch ifError model goto refused else goto modelled
collectTest at modelled do newValues
collectTest at modelled do newCalls
collectTest at modelled do newLabels
collectTest at modelled do newSteps
collectTest at modelled do check
collectTest at modelled branch ifError check goto refused else goto counts
collectTest at counts do countValues
collectTest at counts do expectValues
collectTest at counts do countCalls
collectTest at counts do expectCalls
collectTest at counts do countLabels
collectTest at counts do expectLabels
collectTest at counts do countSteps
collectTest at counts do expectSteps
collectTest at counts do findLimit
collectTest at counts branch ifError findLimit goto refused else goto limitFound
collectTest at limitFound do limitOrigin
collectTest at limitFound do expectConstant
collectTest at limitFound do limitCode
collectTest at limitFound do expectInt64
collectTest at limitFound do findLoop
collectTest at limitFound branch ifError findLoop goto refused else goto loopFound
collectTest at loopFound do loopBounded
collectTest at loopFound do expectBounded
collectTest at loopFound do findPrint
collectTest at loopFound branch ifError findPrint goto refused else goto printFound
collectTest at printFound do printRaises
collectTest at printFound do expectRaises
collectTest at printFound do findSquare
collectTest at printFound branch ifError findSquare goto refused else goto squareFound
collectTest at squareFound do squareArity
collectTest at squareFound do expectTwo
collectTest at squareFound return ok none
collectTest at refused do failRefused
collectTest at refused return ok none

